# The bound is read anew in every iteration: nothing tells that it is a number, and the relation may run other code, which the typed version is left at. It is asked for a number,
# so it is read and rounded before the loop. If the typed version contains other code anyway, the bound is not read.
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}}testedType=number
# CHECK: IntegerBound {{*}}comparison=Less
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 3
# ANSWERS-NEXT: 1
# ANSWERS-NEXT: 2
